Hi all,

Thank you to everyone who took part in Tuesday's flood exercise. This is
a short summary for those who could not attend; the full write-up will
follow after the debrief.

We simulated the river at Weir Bridge rising through the warning stage
and on to the emergency stage over about three hours. As a reminder, the
warning stage starts at 3.8 m and the emergency stage at 4.4 m.

The main finding is that putting up the barriers took 47 minutes across
both stations, against the 40 minute target. Most of the delay came from
loading the posts at the Quayside depot, where the sections are stacked
behind the portable pumps. We will re-arrange the store so the barrier
kit comes out first.

The switchover of the harbour district to Hollow Lane went smoothly.
Pressure in the harbour stayed above 2.5 bar throughout, and no customer
would have noticed anything.

Two actions for now: crew leaders, please check that every member of
your crew has a lifejacket that fits, and duty managers, please confirm
your contact details on the roster by Friday.

Best regards,
Ilse

